id: rust.tokio-broadcast
kind: rust
title: tokio::sync::broadcast
aliases: broadcast channel, fan out
tags: async, channels
questions:
  - how do you send one message to many consumers?
invariant: Every subscriber receives every message, and a subscriber that falls behind gets Lagged instead of slowing the producer down.
answer_30s: broadcast is fan-out: each subscriber sees each message, and lag is reported as an error the consumer must handle rather than blocking senders.
answer_2m: |
  The lagged semantics are the discipline: unlike mpsc, a broadcast send never
  waits for the slowest consumer, so Lagged(n) must be treated as "I missed n
  messages, resynchronise from the source of truth" rather than ignored. That is
  exactly why broadcast fits notifications, cache invalidation and shutdown
  announcements, and does not fit durable work. Each receiver is an independent
  stream, so it is also the natural primitive for propagating config changes to
  running tasks.
when_to_use:
  - notifications, invalidation, shutdown announcements, fan-out where loss is acceptable
avoid_when:
  - work that must not be lost, per-message acknowledgement, competing consumers
minimal_example: |
  use tokio::sync::broadcast;

  let (tx, _) = broadcast::channel::<Event>(64);
  let mut sub = tx.subscribe();

  tokio::spawn(async move {
      loop {
          match sub.recv().await {
              Ok(ev) => handle(ev),
              Err(broadcast::error::RecvError::Lagged(n)) => {
                  tracing::warn!(n, "missed events, resyncing");
                  resync().await;
              }
              Err(broadcast::error::RecvError::Closed) => break,
          }
      }
  });

  let _ = tx.send(Event::ConfigChanged); // never blocks on a slow subscriber
failure_modes:
  - ignoring Lagged, so consumers silently miss updates
  - using broadcast as a work queue, losing jobs whenever it lags
related:
  - rust.tokio-mpsc
  - rust.tokio-watch
  - design.cache-invalidation
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/sync/broadcast/index.html
